{
    "pageid": 107,
    "title": "Moral authority",
    "sections": [
        {
            "heading": "Introduction",
            "level": 1,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Moral authority is an abstraction of a religion 's strength, unity, and respect. Moral authority levels are visible in the Ledger or by hovering the religion icon on any character sheet. Your own religion's moral authority is also visible in the Religion tab, along with its causes."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Effects",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "High moral authority increases the speed and success rate of most types of religious conversion , including the likelihood of Pagans accepting foreign preachers. It also increases the size of holy orders . Low moral authority makes the rise and spread of heresy more likely."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Some religious actions require a minimum moral authority:\n5% to call Great holy wars ,\n40% to issue excommunications ,\n50% to sanction invasions ,\n50% to reform a pagan religion without control of all holy sites"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Modifiers",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Moral authority is primarily affected by control of holy sites and success or failure in religious wars. The personal qualities of the religious head (if there is one) also matter. Below is a full list of factors that affect moral authority:"
